# NUC-32: per-job override for agent_propose.sh (AGENT_JOB_OVERRIDES). Non-secret
# task wiring only — API keys stay in the canonical secrets.env, sourced first.
#
# EXAMPLE ONLY. The live file lives OUTSIDE git at
#   ~/.config/agent-workforce/m1_signal_scan.env  (mode 600, owned by dave)
# and is intentionally NOT committed — mirrors bd_stall_radar.env exactly.
# Install: copy the vars below into that path, then chmod 600.
#
# 2026-07-24: M1 runtime swapped from hermes/claudius (OpenRouter) to headless
# Claude Code (Sonnet, box subscription) while the OpenRouter budget is paused,
# and cadence raised to Mon+Wed (systemd/m1-signal-scan.timer). agent_propose.sh
# is runtime-agnostic — it just execs AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD — so only these three
# lines change. To revert to claudius/OpenRouter: restore the .bak of the live
# file and reset the timer to `OnCalendar=Mon 05:30`.
AGENT_PROFILE=claude-sonnet
AGENT_TASK_SLUG=m1-signal-scan
# Optional: cap retries so a transient failure doesn't triple-run an expensive
# Claude Code research pass (default is 3).
AGENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/run_m1_signal_scan_cc.sh'

# --- Previous runtime (hermes/claudius on OpenRouter), kept for easy revert ---
# AGENT_PROFILE=claudius
# AGENT_TASK_SLUG=m1-signal-scan
# AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='cd ~/agent-worktrees/inbox && ~/.local/bin/hermes -z "$(cat ~/agent-workforce/profiles/m1_signal_scan_task.md)" -p claudius'
